.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="All three integrators here advance the same eccentric two-body Kepler orbit (~physicskit.classical.systems.newtonian.KeplerSystem, semi-major axis a=1, eccentricity e=0.6), i.e. the same Hamiltonian H(q,p) and the same Hamilton&#x27;s equations \dot q = \partial H/\partial p,\ \dot p = -\partial H/\partial q; only the numerical scheme used to step them forward differs. Velocity Verlet updates the separable H = T(p) + V(q) by">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/classical/integrators/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_symplectic_vs_rk4_thumb.png
